content.text:
Finding submitted.

**Status: deviation (critical)** — Section 20 contained only a one-way, unbounded Customer-to-Vendor indemnity ("every claim relating in any way to Customer's use of the Services") and no Vendor indemnity at all, which is walk-away territory under INDEMN. Section 9.3 also cross-referenced infringement remedies in a "Section 20.5" that did not exist.

The validated redline (preferred position):
- **20.1** narrowed to Customer-provided content and Customer's breach of Applicable Law;
- **20.2** Vendor defence/indemnity for third-party IP infringement, breach of law, Vendor-caused Customer Data breach, and gross negligence/wilful misconduct;
- **20.3** standard notice, control, settlement-consent and cooperation mechanics;
- **20.4** usual infringement exclusions (Customer modifications, combinations, Customer specifications);
- **20.5** procure/modify/replace, else terminate and refund — which also repairs the Section 9.3 cross-reference.
